WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.976 --> 00:00:03.132
-My next guest is
a Grammy winner

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:05.467
and a Tony-nominated actress
who stars in

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.701
the new HBO Max series
"Made For Love,"

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.601
which will begin streaming
new episodes tomorrow.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.267
Please welcome Cristin Milioti!

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:14.834
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:19.033
-♪ Cristin Milioti ♪

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:23.300
♪ That's the girl
we're all thinkin' of ♪

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.100
♪ Cristin Milioti ♪
-You look great.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.534
Welcome. Please.
-Thank you.

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:30.767
-That's it.
You've been on...

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.934
Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:34.367
-Thank you for
coming back to our show...

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.367
-Oh, my God, my pleasure.
-...and doing that silly sketch.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.334
But, also, thank you for --
This is --

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.634
You're the only guest to be
in both studios.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.601
-I know, yeah.
-Live in studio.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.033
That's what I'm talking about.
-Oh, my God, it was my pleasure.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.133
-Thank you.
-My pleasure.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.234
It's so nice to see, like,
a full audience.

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:49.434
-Doesn't it feel great?

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:52.067
I want to talk about
"Made For Love,"

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.234
your HBO Max show.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.300
It's getting great reviews.
Congrats on that.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.667
That's awesome.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:57.667
-It's got to feel good.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:00.300
I mean, we were
saying backstage,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.868
because I saw a picture of you

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.300
in front of a giant billboard
in Times Square.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.634
-Yeah.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.400
-And you took a picture -- Or
who took that picture?

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.801
-My showrunner and I --
Christina Lee --

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.334
we went up to Times Square
because we heard

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.934
there was going to be a
billboard for like 45 minutes,

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:16.367
'cause it's electronic, so they,
like, switch through it.

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.601
And so we raced up with
sippy cups full of wine

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.367
to just, like, celebrate it.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.367
-Yeah, that's what
it's all about.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.534
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.133
-I love this photo,
'cause I just love

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.767
anyone who's excited
and appreciative also,

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:28.968
but this photo I liked
almost even more,

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.167
'cause once you're in
Times Square --

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.467
-Yeah. You got to get
the characters in there.

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:35.601
-Times Square Elmo
and a couple of Mickey Mouses.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.634
-And there's the Elmo,
there's the Mickey,

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.634
and then there's, like, the
Mickey that's, like,

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.200
on an off day,
going to the mall,

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.601
just, like,
wearing a coat with a purse.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.067
-I love that Mickey's, like,
got a coat and a purse.

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.634
-But they kept being like,
"Well, You don't want --

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:49.968
No, you don't want
that poster in the back.

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:51.234
Like, here's the better angle."

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:54.367
And then we kept being like,
"Uh, we do, sorry."

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.033
-"Dude, that's
me," without saying that.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.167
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.267
But we were, like,
in front of it,

00:01:58.267 --> 00:01:59.367
and we had our arms
around each other

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:00.801
and we were like,
"Wow, way to go.

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.367
Like, Man, what a journey."

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.934
And then we saw it
go like, "Beep!"

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.968
And we saw someone's laptop,
and they, like,

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:08.767
scrolled the pointer over
and, like, basic--

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:11.200
didn't throw it in the trash,
but, basically --

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.367
And it was a real, like --
the two of us standing there

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.834
being like, "Oh, show biz."

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.834
-Yeah, that's
show business right for you.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.400
That's a very New York
kind of moment, right?

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.767
-Yeah. Yeah.
-You're a New Yorker. Sorry.

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:20.834
-I'm a New Yorker.

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:22.400
-Are you so happy
to see it coming back?

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.567
-So happy.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.534
I just took the subway
for the first time.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:26.601
-You did?
-Yeah.

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:28.467
-What was it like?
-It was beautiful.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:32.501
I, like, put my, like,
subway music in,

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:36.133
and I, like, always am
blasting music on the subway.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.567
And I almost started crying,
it was so beautiful.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.901
Just that we were, like,
all back in there together.

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:41.067
-Yeah.

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.234
-But it wasn't --
I mean, obviously, it's not

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:43.968
at the level that, like --
I miss --

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.767
And I know we'll get back
to this, like,

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:48.534
the full, full, like, subway,

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:51.167
like, "I'm on a New York subway.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:52.200
It's crowded."

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.033
-Yeah.
And some people are touching me.

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.834
-Some people are
touching me, yeah.

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.534
I would always try to
not touch the poles.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:00.334
I would try to, like, surf,
which no one like.

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:01.801
-Oh! Dangerous.

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.334
-It's very rude.
I wouldn't do it now,

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:05.033
'cause when I was, like,
in my early 20s,

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.200
I'd be like, "I bet you I can't
touch the pole!"

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.634
I bet you I can."
And then I was like -- Yeah.

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:09.767
-Would you fall down?

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:12.367
-Yeah, one time,
I was headed to a rehearsal

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:14.801
and I had, like, a, you know,
big bagel and cream cheese

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:16.234
and I was, like,
trying to do that thing,

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:18.434
'cause it's, like, germs, too,
but also, like, I was like,

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:19.868
"I live here."

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:22.467
And I would, like, try to, like,
surf it, like, with the stop.

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:23.501
-Yeah.

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.000
-And so I would use like
one ankle bone

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.767
against, like, the thing.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:29.067
And then I was, like, trying to
eat the bagel and cream cheese,

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:32.801
and they, like,
stopped short, and I fell,

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.701
but I was able to, like,
hold it up,

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.567
and I got it all over
my neck and hair.

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.501
But I was, like,
on my back, like, in the

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.767
grossest, like, stickiest
subway car.

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:41.968
But I was able to
save the bagel,

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.300
and then everyone applauded.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.968
-That's New York!
-Yeah, I know.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.567
-That is New York right there.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.400
-That's New York. I know.
-That is New York.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.267
-I'm very excited
to get back to that.

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:52.734
-Let's talk about
"Made For Love."

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.133
Congrats on the reviews,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.834
but, also,
it's such a cool concept.

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.834
-Yeah.
-Is that what sold you on it?

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:02.200
-Yeah. I mean, when I read it,
I'd never read anything like it.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.267
It's very hard to describe.
It's like --

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.234
-It's funny.

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:07.834
-Yeah.
-But it's sci-fi.

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:09.267
-Yeah.
-And it's twisted.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:10.567
-Yeah.
-Okay, good.

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:12.100
-Yeah. When I try to
describe it,

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.534
do you know that
YouTube video of, like,

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:14.667
the little boy
who's trying to describe --

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:16.000
He's trying to ask a question.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.334
He's like, "Did you ever --
Did you see with the --

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:21.501
And you liked it so much that
you could do anything?"

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:23.567
Like, it's like that whenever
I try to describe it.

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:25.968
I'm like, "It's comedy
and it's also a survivor story

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:28.367
and it's also dark, it's also
twisted, it's also sci-fi.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:31.267
Please just watch it."

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.701
But It's great. I love it.
I mean, I love it.

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.968
But it is like -- You know,
people might not trust you

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:37.634
if you're like, "Just trust me!

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.000
It's good."
-Oh, it works. It's good.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.667
-But it does -- It has --
It's one of the things

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:43.567
I really loved about it is that
it had so many different genres

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:46.467
that I just hadn't ever seen
anything like that.

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:47.868
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:51.133
Here's Cristin Milioti and
Ray Romano in "Made For Love."

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:52.434
Take a look at this.

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:55.567
-I need you to pay
a little more respect to Diane.

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:59.234
♪♪

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:03.000
It is what it is.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.701
She's part of the family.

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:12.868
-Enlighten me on how this works.

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.267
Do you take a bite
out of her food

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:15.767
and then pretend
that she ate it?

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:24.067
Oh.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:26.534
Is it ruined if I do it?

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:31.801
-Cristin Milioti!

